Z||000000||Eric_PA||04-19-2001||10:19 PM||||I recently got a hold of a 3800 series I engine. It was in decent shape, but I decided to tear it down and do a rebuild on it. I am having a very hard time finding performance parts for this thing. The engine is a 1990 Vin C with a roller cam. Anyone know where I could look for better pistons, cam, or roller rockers. I also plan to get the heads ported. Any suggestions would definitely be appreciated. <P>Thanks <BR>Eric<P>* Black 86 ratmatic GT Fastback ---&gt;In the next century hopefully to a 3800 5 speed.<BR>* Red 84 4 speed||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||04-19-2001||10:40 PM||||Hey Eric!<BR>You are in the same boat that I am in...<BR>I have an 87 3800 that I want to hop up...<BR>Nothing drastic, just increased performance with good reliabillity... <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A> <BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||04-20-2001||06:40 AM||||Fierowrecker, It looks like I may be doing a stock rebuild on this engine besides porting and polishing. I think with your 87 3800, you can get a cam from Engle Racing Cams. I tried them, but I was told that since I have a roller lifter setup they can't help me out. I am going to head up to a local machine shop today to look for some suggestions. I'll let you know if I find anything in my travels. Thanks for the reply.<BR>Eric ||||reg||7
